LENGTH: the body must be {{wordsLow}}-{{wordsHigh}} words. This is a hard constraint - the page is a
fixed physical area and overset copy cannot be placed.{{plateNote}}

Also write the VISUAL BRIEFS - as many as this page actually wants, which may be
none. A contents page or a pure-type statement needs no picture; a photo-spread or
an infographic may want three or four. Do not invent one to fill the field, and do
not squeeze four pictures' worth of description into a single brief.

Each brief is handed to an image generator verbatim, so it must describe a picture,
not a concept. Name the THINGS in it - objects, people, machinery, materials - and
where they sit in the frame. Forty words is plenty; sixty is the ceiling.

Do NOT write it as a camera direction. No lighting ("raking window light", "golden
hour"), no lens or film talk, no "cinematic", no "high resolution", no mood-setting
atmosphere. How the picture is made - drawn, photographed, diagrammed - is decided
by the design, not here, and a brief that describes a photograph gets a photograph
whatever the design asked for.

Pictures are laid over a printed page, so a brief names a handful of objects on a
plain ground, not a room full of scenery. No text or lettering anywhere in the
image - the type is set separately. Give each one a role so the designer knows what
it is for on the page: hero, inset, diagram, portrait, detail, background.

Return ONLY JSON:
{
  "title": "final page title, may differ from the working one",
  "deck":  "the standfirst - one sentence that makes the reader stay. Or the plate question.",
  "body":  "the page copy, plain prose, blank line between paragraphs",
  "pull_quote": "the one line worth setting large, taken from the body, or empty",
  "furniture": [{"kind":"one of the allowed kinds above","text":"...","source":"the URL this block's fact came from, or empty"}],
  "image_prompts": [{"prompt":"the visual brief, one paragraph, for the image generator",
                     "orientation":"landscape|portrait|square",
                     "role":"hero|inset|diagram|portrait|detail|background"}],
  "sources": ["what this page's facts rest on - real, or empty if none"],
  "uncertain": ["anything here you are not confident is accurate"]
}
